          "_label": "Details (Official List Description)"
        }
      ],
      "content": "KINGS LANGLEY          \tRED LION LANE TL 00 SE    \t\t\t\t\t(North side)                                     7/245                                   \tLock House No. 68 -                                       \ton Grand Union Canal GV                                      \tII Canal lock keeper's house. Early C19. For Grand Junction Canal Company (became Grand Union Canal by amalgamation 1929), colourwashed brick with hipped slate roof.  2 storeys, 2 windows wide facing E. Small upper windows with recessed sashes, 3/3 panes and segmental arches. Taller similar window to left of door. Canted bay window to RH with 2/2 panes sash windows. Half-glazed panelled door renewed. House stands next lock on W has a half storey below the level of the lock walkway due to the embankment, and a rear extension on the flat. Listing NGR: TL0686404576"
    }
  ],
